### =========================================================================
### Treatment service - requests straight to the service
###
###   @treatment :8082   the Treatment service, own database (treatment.database)
###   @monolith  :8080   the monolith, for comparing the two databases
###
### The Treatment service reads the JWT from the Authorization header only,
### because its sole caller is the monolith. Mint a token as described at the
### top of IsoTreatment.http. It never checks whether the user exists: it
### trusts the user id in the token the monolith has already validated.
### =========================================================================

@monolith = http://localhost:8080
@treatment = http://localhost:8082
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Swagger  ->  200
GET {{treatment}}/swagger/index.html

### Reminders without a token  ->  401
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder

### List  ->  200
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create  ->  200 {"id":N,"time":"08:00:00"}  (full precision; the monolith formats "08:00" for the frontend)
POST {{treatment}}/api/reminder
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "time": "08:00"
}

### Get one  ->  200
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update  ->  200
PUT {{treatment}}/api/reminder/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "time": "21:15"
}

### Delete  ->  204
DELETE {{treatment}}/api/reminder/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Missing reminder  ->  404 "Reminder not found", plain text, no Content-Type
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### =========================================================================
### One owner of the data
###
### Since the switch the monolith has no reminders of its own: whatever goes
### in through it is stored by the Treatment service. Before Phase 8 the same
### pair of reads returned different lists, one per database.
### =========================================================================

### Create through the monolith (cookie)
POST {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "time": "07:45"
}

### Read through the monolith  ->  contains "07:45"
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Read through treatment  ->  contains "07:45:00", the same reminder
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### =========================================================================
### Authentication edge cases
### =========================================================================

### Token in the cookie  ->  401, the service does not read cookies
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Malformed token  ->  401
GET {{treatment}}/api/reminder
Authorization: Bearer not.a.jwt
